  "slug": "why",
  "name": "Why",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Combat cognitive debt from Claude AI-assisted development",
  "longDescription": "Ships **1 skill**, `why` (WHY combats cognitive debt from AI-assisted coding by quizzing developers on implementations they just received).\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install why@claude-community` from `jobrien874/why-plugin`.\n\nWHY is a Claude Code plugin that questions/quizzes you on code you've accepted from Claude in Terminal. Instead of accepting instantly and moving on, you spend 60 seconds confirming you actually understand what was implemented. This may seem extreme to some, but there is a fundemental reason for it which I will get into below.",
